course: dictionary
lesson: 9038
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning the writer wants. Slaughter is one of these words. «Animals are slaughtered on farms to make meat» uses it to mean killing animals for food.
explain: The same word can also describe terrible events. In history lessons, slaughter means the cruel killing of many people, for example in a battle. Clues like battle, war or many people tell you this is the meaning to use.
explain: In sport, slaughter is an informal word for a very easy win or a very heavy defeat. «We got slaughtered 8–0» does not mean anyone was killed. Ask yourself: could this really happen in the sentence? If not, look for the informal meaning.
fact: Slaughter can be a verb (to slaughter) or a noun (the slaughter of animals).
fact: To slaughter animals means to kill them for food, under rules about animal welfare.
fact: To slaughter many people means to kill them cruelly, for example in a war. It is a very serious word, so it is used in history and news.
fact: «Like lambs to the slaughter» means going into danger without knowing it.
fact: Informal: to get slaughtered in sport means to be beaten very easily.
exercise: «Animals are slaughtered on farms to make meat.» What does slaughtered mean here? | To keep animals warm in winter | To sell animals at a fair | *To kill animals for food | To look after animals until they are old
exercise: «We got slaughtered 8–0 in the match.» What does slaughtered mean in this sentence? | *Lost very badly | Scored eight goals ourselves | Won a gold medal | Played in the rain all afternoon
exercise: Which sentence uses slaughter for the cruel killing of many people? | The farm sold its lambs at the market | We played a fun game of tag | The baker made a huge chocolate cake | *The battle ended in terrible slaughter
test: «Went to the glue factory» is a joking way to say what? | *An old horse was slaughtered | A horse was painted | A farm was sold to a new owner | A cow won a prize at the show
test: What does «like lambs to the slaughter» mean? | *Going into danger without knowing it | Being very gentle with animals | Playing a game of football | Jumping for joy
exam: Which is the best meaning of slaughtered in «Processed means farm animals were slaughtered for meat»? | To mend a broken fence | To feed animals well | To sell animals in a shop | *To kill animals for meat
